---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import StageSequence from '../components/StageSequence.astro';
import ProofPoint from '../components/ProofPoint.astro';
import CTAButton from '../components/CTAButton.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Google Distributed Cloud"
  description="C-9INE helps banks, government institutions and critical-infrastructure organisations turn Google Distributed Cloud into a secure, production-ready operating platform."
>
  <!--
    This page's structure and copy follow the C-9INE GDC Executive Booklet
    (v1.0) page for page: Problem, Belief, How It Works, What We
    Standardise, Customer Outcomes, in that order, including its own
    headline wording where it exists. See docs/content-brief.md §4 for
    the earlier hero-wording sign-off note this supersedes.
  -->
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Google Distributed Cloud">
    <h1>One platform. Less chaos.</h1>
    <p class="gdc-subhead">Run VMs and containers on your infrastructure with a cloud operating model.</p>
    <p class="lede">
      Your infrastructure. Cloud operating model. Sovereign control. C-9INE helps banks,
      government and critical-infrastructure organisations turn Google Distributed Cloud into a
      secure, production-ready operating platform — covering everything from readiness to
      capability transfer.
    </p>
    <div class="page-intro__cta">
      <CTAButton href="/contact?intent=gdc-pilot">Book a GDC pilot scoping call</CTAButton>
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="section-tight stage-section">
    <div class="container">
      <StageSequence
        stages={['Problem', 'Belief', 'How it works', 'Standardise', 'Outcomes']}
        eyebrow="C-9INE Engineering Story"
      >
        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">01</span>
          <h3>Your data centre was not meant to become this complicated.</h3>
          <p>
            VMware, Nutanix, Hyper-V, Kubernetes and cloud projects often grow into separate
            platforms, each with its own skills and operating model.
          </p>

          <ol class="numbered-rows">
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">01</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Licensing pressure</h4>
                <p>Renewals, bundles and platform overlap make budgeting harder.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">02</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Platform sprawl</h4>
                <p>Different stacks create different tools, teams and runbooks.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">03</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Skills fragmentation</h4>
                <p>Specialists are spread across too many operating models.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">04</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Operational overhead</h4>
                <p>Security, compliance and lifecycle controls are repeated in each stack.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p class="statement">
            More platforms did not create simplicity. They created another operating problem.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">02</span>
          <h3>Modernisation should reduce complexity, not move it somewhere else.</h3>
          <p>
            Google Distributed Cloud brings a cloud operating model to infrastructure you
            control, so VMs and containers can move in one strategic direction.
          </p>

          <div class="plus-row">
            <span class="plus-row__item">VMs</span>
            <span class="plus-row__sign">+</span>
            <span class="plus-row__item">Containers</span>
            <span class="plus-row__sign">+</span>
            <span class="plus-row__item">Policy</span>
            <span class="plus-row__sign">+</span>
            <span class="plus-row__item">Operations</span>
          </div>

          <p class="statement">One platform for legacy workloads and modern applications.</p>

          <p>
            The platform experience matters because you need a controlled path from today's
            estate to tomorrow's cloud model.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">03</span>
          <h3>From fragmented estates to a single operating model.</h3>
          <p>
            A practical path that translates today's infrastructure into repeatable GDC
            architecture, governance and operations.
          </p>

          <ol class="numbered-rows">
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">01</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Assess</h4>
                <p>Inventory platforms, renewal timing, dependencies and workload fit.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">02</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Consolidate</h4>
                <p>Converge VMs and containers closer to one platform direction.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">03</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Govern</h4>
                <p>Apply consistent policy, security, IAM and lifecycle controls.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">04</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Operate</h4>
                <p>Standardise observability, automation and handover practices.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p class="statement">
            Assess the estate. Consolidate the platform. Govern consistently. Operate with
            confidence.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">04</span>
          <h3>The foundations every GDC programme depends on.</h3>
          <p>
            C-9INE helps industrialise the patterns that are too important to rebuild manually,
            platform by platform.
          </p>

          <ul class="stage-panel__domains">
            <li>
              <svg class="stage-panel__domain-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="12" rx="1.5" />
                <path d="M12,16 L12,20" />
                <path d="M9,20 L15,20" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-label">VM runtime</p>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-desc">Run existing virtual machines under a cloud operating model</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="stage-panel__domain-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <rect x="4" y="4" width="12" height="12" rx="2" />
                <rect x="8" y="8" width="12" height="12" rx="2" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-label">Kubernetes</p>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-desc">Standardise container platform operations</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="stage-panel__domain-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <circle cx="12" cy="5" r="2" />
                <circle cx="5" cy="18" r="2" />
                <circle cx="19" cy="18" r="2" />
                <path d="M12,7 L6.5,16.3" />
                <path d="M12,7 L17.5,16.3" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-label">Networking</p>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-desc">Repeatable connectivity and segmentation patterns</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="stage-panel__domain-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <path d="M12,3 L20,6 L20,12 C20,17 16.5,20.5 12,22 C7.5,20.5 4,17 4,12 L4,6 Z" />
                <path d="M8.5,12 L11,14.5 L16,9" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-label">IAM &amp; access</p>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-desc">Clear roles, permissions and boundaries</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="stage-panel__domain-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <path d="M2,12 C5,6 19,6 22,12 C19,18 5,18 2,12 Z" />
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.5" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-label">Observability</p>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-desc">Logging, monitoring and operational visibility</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg class="stage-panel__domain-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <path d="M6,3 L15,3 L19,7 L19,21 L6,21 Z" />
                <path d="M15,3 L15,7 L19,7" />
                <path d="M9,12 L16,12 M9,15.5 L16,15.5 M9,9 L12,9" />
              </svg>
              <div>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-label">Security &amp; compliance</p>
                <p class="stage-panel__domain-desc">Consistent guardrails and control evidence</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="statement">Standardisation is what turns infrastructure into a platform.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="stage-panel">
          <span class="stage-number">05</span>
          <h3>From infrastructure estate to cloud operating model.</h3>
          <p>
            The goal is not another technology island. The goal is a simpler, governed way to
            run today's workloads while modernising.
          </p>

          <ol class="numbered-rows">
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">01</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Reduce licensing pressure</h4>
                <p>Fewer duplicated platform layers.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">02</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Lower operational overhead</h4>
                <p>One model for VMs and containers.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">03</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Improve skills leverage</h4>
                <p>Common patterns across teams.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">04</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Strengthen control</h4>
                <p>Policy, security and visibility built in.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">05</span>
              <div>
                <h4>Modernise safely</h4>
                <p>Run today's workloads while building tomorrow's apps.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p class="statement">One platform. Less chaos.</p>
        </article>
      </StageSequence>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="why-now">
        <h2>Why now</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Broadcom's acquisition of VMware changed the calculus on every renewal. Most FSI
          estates we work with are already re-evaluating VMware, Nutanix, Hyper-V and Kubernetes
          side by side, not on some future roadmap. Your next hypervisor renewal doesn't have to
          mean renewing the same complexity — it can be the moment you standardise on one
          platform, one policy model, one fleet view, without forcing every workload to
          modernise on day one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="verticals">
        <h2>If your workload is critical, local or regulated</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Not theoretical. These are the institutions we build GDC for, in Saudi Arabia today.
        </p>

        <div class="verticals__grid">
          <div class="verticals__card">
            <h4>Banking &amp; finance</h4>
            <p>
              Sovereign core-adjacent platforms, fraud and AI workloads kept local, VM
              consolidation off ageing hypervisors.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="verticals__card">
            <h4>Government</h4>
            <p>
              Citizen services, national data custody, one secure platform standard instead of
              several.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="verticals__card">
            <h4>Healthcare</h4>
            <p>
              Patient records and private analytics that never have to leave the building,
              resilient local services.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="verticals__card">
            <h4>Critical infrastructure</h4>
            <p>
              Site autonomy, low latency, operational continuity even when connectivity isn't
              guaranteed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="verticals__close">
          If the workload is critical, local, regulated or latency-sensitive, it belongs in this
          conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="modes">
        <h2>Two delivery models. Your regulator chooses.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Software-only or air-gapped. Connected or fully isolated. Every choice on this page
          exists so the decision stays yours, not ours — that's not a compliance requirement,
          it's how we think a vendor should behave. Both are genuine GDC, not a workaround, and
          C-9INE delivers both.
        </p>

        <div class="modes__grid">
          <div class="modes__card">
            <svg class="modes__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M4,10 L4,20 L20,20 L20,10" />
              <path d="M2,10 L12,3 L22,10 Z" />
              <path d="M9,20 L9,14 L15,14 L15,20" />
            </svg>
            <h4>GDC software-only</h4>
            <p class="mono-tag modes__tag">Connected</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Runs on your own supported x86 servers, in your data centre</li>
              <li>A lightweight connect agent registers clusters to your fleet in Google Cloud</li>
              <li>Fastest path to production; reuses your existing hardware investment</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="modes__card">
            <svg class="modes__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M12,3 L20,6 L20,12 C20,17 16.5,20.5 12,22 C7.5,20.5 4,17 4,12 L4,6 Z" />
              <rect x="9" y="11" width="6" height="5" rx="1" />
              <path d="M10.2,11 L10.2,9.2 A1.8,1.8 0 0 1 13.8,9.2 L13.8,11" />
            </svg>
            <h4>GDC air-gapped</h4>
            <p class="mono-tag modes__tag">Fully isolated</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Integrated Google hardware, delivered and installed at your premises</li>
              <li>No connection to Google Cloud or the public internet, by design, ever</li>
              <li>Built for classified and the most stringent sovereignty requirements</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof">
        <ProofPoint eyebrow="Proof">
          Live Saudi GDC delivery, not theoretical: a national regulator, a tier-one commercial
          bank, and a large-scale production rollout.
        </ProofPoint>
        <p class="lede proof__context">
          Delivered in the region's strictest regulatory environment, alongside Google Cloud's
          own Dammam region (me-central2) and the Class C licence CST granted it there.
        </p>

        <div class="proof__grid">
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Regulatory baseline</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              GDC software-only validated against sovereign data, operational compliance and
              security expectations, for a national financial regulator.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Tier-one commercial bank</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Mission-critical legacy applications and microservices coexisting on
              customer-owned infrastructure, in production.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Large-scale production rollout</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Anthos-to-GDC migration path and multi-cluster architecture readiness, delivered
              at scale.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">VM Runtime, in production</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Live at a Saudi bank today — VMs and containers governed under one operating
              model, not a lab environment.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Sovereign AI, natively</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Gemini runs inside the platform, including fully air-gapped, so model inference
              never has to leave the building.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="proof__assets">
          <span class="proof__assets-label mono-tag">Reusable assets</span>
          <div class="proof__tags">
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">HLD/LLD baselines</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">VM Runtime validation</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">Multi-DC bare-metal design</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">Migration factory runbooks</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">Operational handover model</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pilot">
        <h2>Start with a focused pilot, not a leap</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A 4–6 week pilot makes the GDC decision tangible before you commit to a full migration.
          Install and register GDC software-only on your own supported hardware, migrate a
          small representative set of VM and container workloads, and walk away with proof your
          team can run this, not just that we can install it.
        </p>

        <div class="pilot-timeline">
          <div class="pilot-timeline__line" data-reveal></div>
          <ol class="pilot-timeline__steps">
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:0ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">1</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 1</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Executive alignment + target workloads</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:100ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">2</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 2</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">MCDC, inventory + prerequisites</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:200ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">3–4</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Weeks 3–4</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Pilot build + workload migration</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:300ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">5</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 5</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Evidence pack + business case</span>
            </li>
            <li data-reveal style="transition-delay:400ms">
              <span class="pilot-timeline__num mono-tag">6</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__label">Week 6</span>
              <span class="pilot-timeline__desc">Production roadmap + commercials</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="pilot__cards">
          <div class="pilot__card">
            <h4>Example scope</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>4–6 weeks, subject to readiness</li>
              <li>Customer-provided supported bare-metal servers</li>
              <li>Install and register GDC software-only</li>
              <li>Migrate 1 Linux VM + 1 Windows VM</li>
              <li>Migrate 3–5 representative container workloads</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="pilot__card">
            <h4>Success criteria</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Platform installed and healthy</li>
              <li>VM Runtime enabled and validated</li>
              <li>VMs boot, connect and pass application checks</li>
              <li>Containers deploy via agreed manifests / GitOps</li>
              <li>Known gaps and prerequisites documented</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="pilot__card">
            <h4>Commercial outcome</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Confirms technical feasibility for your executives</li>
              <li>Creates a local reference and evidence pack</li>
              <li>Feeds directly into a production HLD/LLD and business case</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pilot__cta">
          <CTAButton href="/contact?intent=gdc-pilot">Book a GDC pilot scoping call</CTAButton>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .gdc-subhead {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  /* Same fix as the Cloud Migration page: the preceding section's own
     bottom padding plus this section's usual top padding compounded
     into a much bigger gap here than anywhere else on the page. */
  .stage-section {
    padding-top: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
  }

  /* The numbered process/outcome lists used inside several stage
     panels (Problem's four causes, How It Works' four steps,
     Outcomes' five results) — a compact variant of the same dark
     numbered-row pattern, sized to fit inside a pinned stage panel
     rather than a full standalone section. */
  .numbered-rows {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--gunmetal-line);
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .numbered-rows li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--gunmetal-raised);
  }

  .numbered-rows__num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--gunmetal);
    color: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  .numbered-rows h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .numbered-rows p {
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* The Belief panel's "VMs + Containers + Policy + Operations" row,
     matching the booklet's own plus-separated block layout. */
  .plus-row {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .plus-row__item {
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 30%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 8%, transparent);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .plus-row__sign {
    color: var(--aquamarine);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* The bold highlight box each booklet page closes on ("More
     platforms did not create simplicity...", "One platform. Less
     chaos.", etc.) — reused across every stage panel that has one. */
  .statement {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 8%, transparent);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .why-now {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .why-now h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .why-now .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .verticals {
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .verticals h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .verticals .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .verticals__grid {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .verticals__card {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
